# Security

- Never commit secrets, tokens, or credentials.
- User scripts run only in `nexus_core::scripts::ScriptSandbox` (fresh QuickJS runtime per run, memory limit, wall-clock interrupt). The only host link is the closure-captured `host(op, argsJson)`; never expose it on the global. No `eval`-style escape hatches to the host.
- HTML preview and the visualizer never embed a webview: the HTML is written to a private temp file (0600) with an injected CSP (preview blocks scripts, visualizer blocks network) and opened in the system browser. Visualizer data is escaped by `nexus_core::visualizer`.
- Validate file names/ids that come from the user or from imported files (`nexus_core::fs::is_safe_file_id`, single-path-component dir names). Never join them into paths unchecked. All writes go through `nexus_core::fs` (0600 files, 0700 dirs).
- TLS verification is on by default; only disable it through the per-request `rejectUnauthorized: false` setting.
- Spawn MCP stdio servers directly (no shell) with a cleared environment plus the allowlist.
- Never log sensitive headers (`Authorization`, `Cookie`, `Set-Cookie`).
